          "id": "test-listening",
          "text": "← 全部测试\n听力整科测试\n\n4 Parts · 40 题 · 完整原音\n\n官方机考体验题 · 40题。选择题可填字母，提交后核对参考答案。\n\n32:00\n继续本次\n提交本次作答\n0% · 0 / 40 已作答\n\n按录音指示完成四个 Part。此处使用官方机考体验题，计时为本地练习计时。\n\nPart 1 · Q1–10\n0% · 0 / 10 已作答\nNote Completion\n\nOne word and/or a number\n\nPhone call about second-hand furniture\n\nItems:\n\nDining table:          - \n[ 1 ______ ]\nshape\n\n                             -  medium size\n\n                             - \n[ 2 ______ ]\nold\n\n                             -  price: £25.00\n\n\nDining chairs:         - set of\n[ 3 ______ ]\nchairs\n\n                              - seats covered in\n[ 4 ______ ]\nmaterial\n\n                              - in\n[ 5 ______ ]\ncondition\n\n                              - price: £20.00\n\n\nDesk:                     - length: 1 metre 20\n\n                              - 3 drawers. Top drawer has a\n[ 6 ______ ]\n.\n                              \n                              - price: £\n[ 7 ______ ]\n\n\n\nAddress:\n[ 8 ______ ]\nOld Lane, Stonethorpe\n\n\n\nDirections:\nTake the Hawcroft road out of Stonethorpe. Go past the secondary school, then turn\n[ 9 ______ ]\nat the crossroads. House is down this road, opposite the\n[ 10 ______ ]\n .\nQ1\nQ2\nQ3\nQ4\nQ5\nQ6\nQ7\nQ8\nQ9\nQ10\nPart 2 · Q11–20\n0% · 0 / 10 已作答\nMatching\n\nWho is responsible for each area?\n\nStaff Responsibilities\n\nA. Finance\nB. Food\nC. Health\nD. Kids' Counselling\nE. Organisation\nF. Rooms\nG. Sport\nH. Trips\nPeople\n\n\nMary Brown [ 11 ______ ]\n\nJohn Stevens [ 12 ______ ]\n\nAlison Jones [ 13 ______ ]\n\nTim Smith [ 14 ______ ]\n\nJenny James [ 15 ______ ]\n\nPlan, Map, Diagram Labelling\n\nA. Cookery room\nB. Games room\nC. Kitchen\nD. Pottery room\nE. Sports complex\nF. Staff accommodation\n[ 16 ______ ]\n[ 17 ______ ]\n[ 18 ______ ]\n[ 19 ______ ]\n[ 20 ______ ]\nQ11\nQ12\nQ13\nQ14\nQ15\nQ16\nQ17\nQ18\nQ19\nQ20\nPart 3 · Q21–30\n0% · 0 / 10 已作答\nMatching\n\nWhich feature do the speakers identify for each of the following categories of fossil?\n\nFeatures\n\nA. They are a very rare type of plant fossil.\nB. They do not contain any organic matter.\nC. They are found in soft, wet ground.\nD. They can be found far from normal fossil areas.\nE. They are three-dimensional.\nF. They provide information about plant cells.\nFossil categories\n\n\nImpression fossils [ 21 ______ ]\n\nCast fossils [ 22 ______ ]\n\nPermineralisation fossils [ 23 ______ ]\n\nCompaction fossils [ 24 ______ ]\n\nFusain fossils [ 25 ______ ]\n\nFlow-chart Completion Objective\n\nA. contamination\nB. vehicle\nC. heat\nD. results\nE. radiation\nF. site\nG. microbes\nH. water\nA spacecraft lands on a planet and sends out a rover.\nThe rover is directed to a [ 26 ______ ] which has organic material.\nIt collects a sample from below the surface (in order to avoid the effects of [ 27 ______ ]).\nThe soil and rocks are checked to look for evidence of fossils.\nThe sample is converted to powder.\nThe sample is subjected to [ 28 ______ ] .\nA mass spectrometer is used to search for potential proof of life, e.g [ 29 ______ ] .\nThe [ 30 ______ ] are compared with existing data from Earth.\nQ21\nQ22\nQ23\nQ24\nQ25\nQ26\nQ27\nQ28\nQ29\nQ30\nPart 4 · Q31–40\n0% · 0 / 10 已作答\nMC Questions\n\nQuestion 31\nParticipants in the Learner Persistence study were all drawn from the same\nA. age group.\nB. geographical area.\nC. socio-economic level.\nQuestion 32\nThe study showed that when starting their course, older students were most concerned about\nA. effects on their home life.\nB. implications for their future career.\nC. financial constraints.\nTable Completion\n\nOne word only\n\n \nResearch findings\n\n         \n\tSocial and Environmental Factors\tOther Factors\tPersonal Characteristics\n  First level of importance\tEffective support\tPerceived success in study\tEnjoyment of a\n[ 33 ______ ]\n\n  Second level of importance\tPositive experiences at\n[ 34 ______ ]\n\tGood\n[ 35 ______ ]\n\tMany\n[ 36 ______ ]\n in daily life\n 